      "at": "2026-11-16T07:50:49.786Z",
      "type": "agent_text",
      "text": "I didn't place an order, because the store couldn't confirm that any dock under $150 runs two 4K 60 Hz displays from a USB-C port.\n\n- **Demo Dock Duo ($129.00):** This is the only possible fit. Its USB-C port check passes, and it has 2 video outputs and 90 W power delivery. The store hasn't listed how many 4K 60 Hz displays it supports (`max_displays_4k60`), so the two-display check came back \"unknown\". I won't buy it without that confirmation.\n- **Demo Dock Duo Lite ($89.00):** Not compatible. It supports only one 4K 60 Hz display.\n- **Demo Dock Solo ($59.00) and Demo Dock Travel ($39.00):** The store lists each with one output and one 4K 60 Hz display, so neither can run two. It didn't run the compatibility check on them.\n\n**What's missing:** the Demo Dock Duo's 4K 60 Hz display count. If the store adds it, I can check again.\n\nI can also check the docks against a different setup, such as one 4K 60 Hz display."
    }
